			<div class="content" id="post-content-2720976">
									

<p>I really like the tone and flavor of this, particularly the interview log in the bookstore. The brief flashes of intent we get from the program, like when it tries to help the agent who says he's in danger, really add to the personality of the piece.</p>
<p>It's too bad that the end stage of this program is terminal database corruption and a breakdown of commerce, because I get the sense that even though it describes itself as a virus it's still trying to serve the customer at the end of the day. +1</p>
<p>EDIT: I didn't check the axis labels on the graph since in my window size they were illegible without maximizing, but on closer inspection buttfranklin is right. This graph would make a lot more sense with the axis labels reversed.</p>

